From: iosbackup maintainers
Subject: afc: return immediately after payload receive failure

The locked upstream revision frees the receive buffer after a failed
service_receive call but then continues into the short-read checks. That can
free the same buffer again or use it later in the function.

--- a/src/afc.c
+++ b/src/afc.c
@@ -313,6 +313,7 @@ static afc_error_t afc_receive_data(afc_client_t client, char **bytes, uint32_t
 		if (err != AFC_E_SUCCESS) {
 			free(buf);
 			debug_info("Failed to receive data: %s (%d)", afc_strerror(err), err);
+			return err;
 		}
 		if (recv_len <= 0) {
 			free(buf);
